---
import SecondaryLayout from '../../layouts/SecondaryLayout.astro';
---
<SecondaryLayout
  title="Features"
  description="Explore Lythaus plans for original perspectives, feed choices, contribution rewards and clear authorship."
  canonicalPath="/features"
>
  <section class="section section--wide">
    <h1>Features</h1>
    <p>
      We’re building Lythaus around original perspectives and thoughtful discussion.
      These are the features we’re developing; availability depends on the rollout.
    </p>

    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Share your perspective</h2>
        <p>
          Share experience, research, creative work and useful questions.
          Follow people whose contributions help you think, and join the discussion.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Choose your feed</h2>
        <p>
          Discovery shows eligible public posts, newest first. Following focuses
          on people you follow. Custom feeds let you choose filters for a more
          focused view.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Recognition and rewards</h2>
        <p>
          Our reputation model values constructive human-authored contributions,
          useful sources and accountable participation. Rewards are in development;
          availability and eligibility will be explained as they roll out.
          Membership payments do not buy reputation or Editorial recognition.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Clear authorship</h2>
        <p>
          Our policy uses Human-authored, AI-assisted and Under review labels.
          Disclosed, human-led AI-assisted text is limited to 249 characters.
          AI-generated public content and AI-assisted images or videos are not
          permitted. Automated authorship signals are being developed to support
          trained human review.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Safety and accountability</h2>
        <p>
          Authorship labels describe how content was made; they are not a safety
          approval or a fact check. Harmful-content rules apply regardless of
          authorship or membership tier. Read our <a href="/guidelines">Community Guidelines</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Appeals process</h2>
        <p>
          During alpha, authorised staff review appeals under our <a href="/terms">Terms</a>.
          The planned process uses independently assigned trained reviewers and
          adjudicators, subject to rollout readiness. It is not an open community vote.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p><a class="button primary" href="/#waitlist">Join the waitlist</a></p>
    <p>Joining does not guarantee an invitation or an access date.</p>
  </section>
</SecondaryLayout>
